      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -3}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{7}⁡(x+3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246608/assets/0b45cd648830ad88c2f21865c1bfd704783a7b5d9ce3510646ae55e98d2d95ac.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\le -3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x>-3.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are not equal, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -3}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
